cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use FireLens or its data, please cite it as below, and cite the NASA
  products it is built on (listed under references).
title: "FireLens: a harmonized MODIS–VIIRS burning-activity calendar for Northern India, 2016–2026"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "COSMICBRO's (FireLens team)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/frbasil-1k/HARMONIZATION-space-app"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-15"
abstract: >-
  FireLens harmonizes active-fire hotspot detections from Terra and Aqua MODIS
  and Suomi-NPP VIIRS into one monthly burning-activity record for 49 districts
  of Punjab, Haryana and Uttarakhand (2016–2026), and serves it as a web
  calendar with anomalies, trends, sensor-range uncertainty and fire-type
  context. Built for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.
keywords:
  - active fire
  - hotspots
  - MODIS
  - VIIRS
  - harmonization
  - crop residue burning
  - NASA Space Apps Challenge
